WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:02.500
Somewhere right now, a customer just asked

00:02.500 --> 00:05.000
ChatGPT to pick a company like yours —

00:05.000 --> 00:08.000
and ChatGPT picked somebody. The question is

00:08.000 --> 00:10.800
whether it even knew you exist.

00:11.500 --> 00:14.500
Search engines stopped handing out lists and started

00:14.500 --> 00:15.900
handing out answers.

00:15.900 --> 00:19.500
SEO ranks you in a list; AEO makes you the answer.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.500
But here's what nobody tells you:

00:22.500 --> 00:25.700
being readable isn't being believable. An AI can

00:25.700 --> 00:29.200
quote your website and still refuse to recommend

00:29.200 --> 00:30.500
your business.

00:30.500 --> 00:31.700
Machines cross-reference.

00:31.700 --> 00:34.700
If your address disagrees with your listing and

00:34.700 --> 00:36.200
your reviews float around

00:36.200 --> 00:38.300
unattached, the machine doesn't argue —

00:38.300 --> 00:40.000
it moves on.

00:40.500 --> 00:42.300
This is where SignalFlair wins.

00:42.300 --> 00:43.500
Instead of guessing, it measures —

00:43.500 --> 00:47.000
a Signal Score from zero to one hundred, showing exactly how

00:47.000 --> 00:48.700
visible and trustworthy you look to AI.

00:48.700 --> 00:50.900
The fix is infrastructure, not vibes:

00:51.000 --> 00:54.000
a crawlable Signal Proof page, machine-readable files like

00:54.000 --> 00:56.000
llms.txt and proof.json —

00:56.000 --> 00:57.500
assets an AI can actually inspect.

00:57.500 --> 01:00.000
So: SEO gets you found in a list,

01:00.000 --> 01:03.000
AEO gets you used in an answer,

01:03.000 --> 01:05.000
and SignalFlair gets you verified —

01:05.000 --> 01:06.500
the part the other two depend on.

01:06.500 --> 01:09.000
Because AI doesn't warn you before it checks.

01:09.000 --> 01:11.500
Stay ready, so you don't have to get ready.
